reason = 0.66b2 declares wrapt ~= 1.0, which is the only term in the injected
    tree that rejects wrapt 2.x, and one rejected line stands the whole
    distribution down. open-telemetry/opentelemetry-python-contrib#5117 widened
    the requirement to wrapt >= 1.0.0, < 3.0.0 on 2026-10-01, after the 0.66
    patch branch had split, so no 0.66 release carries it. The source here is
    the v0.66b2 source verbatim; only the requirement changes.
removal = Every step. Only two of them fail CI on their own, the wheel-contents
    step and uv lock --check; the rest leave dead code or stale prose that
    nothing catches. Grep the repository for asyncclick afterwards. The hits
    left should be CHANGELOG.rst, .chloggen, uv.lock, and the docstring of
    test_wrapt_accepts_what_opentelemetry_instrumentation_declares in
    packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_all_dependencies_manifest.py, which
    records why that line asserts what it does and stays true afterwards.

    Delete this directory. In packages/dash0-opentelemetry/pyproject.toml,
    restore opentelemetry-instrumentation-asyncclick to [project].dependencies,
    drop the [project.optional-dependencies] instruments table, drop the
    asyncclick entry under [project.entry-points.opentelemetry_instrumentor],
    drop the asyncclick and anyio entries of the dev dependency group, and set
    [tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel] packages back to ["src/dash0"].

    Drop the three asyncclick paths from the wheel-contents step of
    .github/workflows/ci.yml, keeping the test-against-wrapt-2 job, which is not
    asyncclick-specific and keeps its value once the dependency returns. Drop
    the asyncclick exclusion from ruff.toml, and the asyncclick entry of
    EXEMPT_FROM_EXACT_PIN in scripts/check_pinned_dependencies.py together with
    the tests naming asyncclick in scripts/tests/test_check_pinned_dependencies.py.

    Drop the dash0-opentelemetry key of
    upstream_packages_shadowed_by_shipped_packages in sitecustomize.py, and in
    packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_sitecustomize.py both the
    opentelemetry-instrumentation-asyncclick entry of the shadowed list and the
    make_dist("dash0-opentelemetry", ...) entry of
    shipped_distributions_that_shadow_upstream. Drop the
    VENDORED_INSTRUMENTATIONS entry and the import it is built from in
    packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_instrumentations.py, which leaves
    the dict empty and makes every test in that module compare whole sets again.
    Delete packages/dash0-opentelemetry/tests/test_vendored_asyncclick.py.

    Drop the asyncclick paragraph from docs/auto-instrumentation.md, the
    asyncclick row and the paragraph under it from docs/kubernetes-injection.md,
    the asyncclick deviation bullet from packages/dash0-opentelemetry/README.rst,
    asyncclick's name from the project-layout bullet of CONTRIBUTING.rst, and
    from the root CLAUDE.md the second
    derivation command with the paragraph under it, the clause about
    instrumentations carried as source, and asyncclick's name in the list of
    vendored paths.

    Then run uv lock, which the uv lock --check job requires, and regenerate
    all-dependencies.txt.
